cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProseCast or build on its attribution, casting or actioning-tag design, please cite it."
title: "ProseCast: local-first full-cast audiobooks with speaker attribution, casting, and actioning-verb delivery tags"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koontz
    given-names: Tyler
repository-code: "https://github.com/Koontzie/prosecast"
license: GPL-3.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
version: 0.9.0
keywords:
  - audiobook
  - text-to-speech
  - speaker attribution
  - dialogue attribution
  - voice casting
  - actioning
  - local-first
abstract: >-
  ProseCast turns a book the user owns into a multi-voice audiobook on the
  user's own machine. It attributes dialogue to speakers with a rule cascade
  plus a local language model, records every human correction as labeled
  data, lets the user cast a voice per character, tags each line with an
  actor's playable intention (an actioning verb, intensity and pace) stored
  independently of the speech engine, and renders locally.
